  "notes": "Swedish dance-pop with a trance-derived lead. `confidence` is low because the research rates the entry medium-low: \"era and Swedish dance-pop positioning documented; parameters trance-pop convention and marked\", and the harmony claim carries an explicit `[LOW-CONF]` which is repeated here. What the entry does state drives three things. \"The kick is de-emphasised relative to the bass, per the trance convention\" — a lower accent tier than the hands-up models and a continuous rolling 16th bass at 0.94 roots. \"Snare rolls into the drop\" — an authored roll ramp with the ladder on. And \"toplines are bright, high, unornamented and singable — written to work equally as an instrumental anthem\", which is a high, low-density, stepwise melody over 8-bar loops with the supersaw doubling or answering it. Percussion is minimal because the record is lead-and-bass. ⚠ Every velocity, density and probability above is INFERRED from those sentences; the tempo band is the entry's and the four-on-the-floor/clap-on-2&4 pair is the entry's.",
